{#
    Written to /etc/rc.conf.d/ctrld. This is the rcvar step -- separate from
    ctrld's own rc.d script existing -- so that installing/enabling this
    plugin actually persists ctrld across reboots via the standard OPNsense
    model -> configd -> rc.conf.d pattern, rather than assuming package
    presence implies boot persistence.

    helpers.getNodeByTag(...), not direct OPNsense.ctrld.general.enabled
    dot-chain access -- same fix, same reason, as ctrld.toml's [service]
    block (see that file's header comment for the full explanation).
    Matters even more here: this template is +TARGETS-ordered before
    ctrld.toml, so on a fresh install (General never saved) an
    UndefinedError here would fail the whole `template reload` before
    ctrld.toml even got a chance to render.
#}
ctrld_enable="{% if helpers.getNodeByTag('OPNsense.ctrld.general.enabled') == '1' %}YES{% else %}NO{% endif %}"
